zerch (0.7.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * TUI: searching now shows a vim-style notice on the prompt line (in pink) when
    a search wraps past an end of the file — "Search reached BOTTOM, continuing
    from TOP" for "/"/"n", and the reverse for "?"/"N". The notice clears on the
    next keypress.
  * TUI: a --view string (hand-edited, stale, or from a since-truncated file) that
    names bookmarks, revealed ranges, hidden lines, or a selected line past the end
    of the file no longer conjures phantom rows beyond EOF — such out-of-range line
    references are now dropped when the view is applied.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.7.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * TUI: search now starts from the cursor instead of the top of the file. "/"
    jumps to the first match at or after the cursor (wrapping if none ahead), and
    a new "?" searches backward; "n" repeats in the search direction and "N"
    reverses it.
  * TUI: "?" no longer opens the help overlay — ":help" (or ":h") does. The help
    overlay was rewritten to cover every key, including the menu and the time
    histogram, which it had omitted.
  * TUI: pressing "x" to hide a line now always moves the cursor to the next
    exposed line (never onto the collapsed gap), so repeated "x" hides consecutive
    lines starting with the first.
  * TUI: the ":" command line now keeps its own recallable history (up/down),
    separate from the search/filter/highlight term history.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.7.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * TUI: new zebra-striping display toggle (menu "z") — a faint tint on alternate
    logical lines, mirroring the web UI. The tint runs to the right edge of the
    row. Off by default.
  * TUI: the syntax-colour, filter-colour, and zebra display toggles are now
    remembered per file across sessions (saved in the view token).
  * TUI: toggling a bookmark, hiding a line, or revealing a gap no longer re-runs
    the whole-file filter search — the cached filter result is reused — removing a
    noticeable pause on multi-million-line files.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.7.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * TUI: filter terms are now coloured from the same palette as highlights, assigned
    by position so filter and highlight colours never overlap (up to the palette
    size). Each filter's term is boxed in its own colour in the rendered line, the
    m menu shows a colour swatch per filter, and a new "l" toggle turns filter
    colouring on and off (on by default).

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Sun, 14 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.7.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * TUI: an active filter's term is now highlighted in place in the rendered line
    (a light-blue box, the same treatment as an 'h' highlight and matching the web
    UI), in both the list and JSON views. Precedence is search > highlight > filter;
    disabled, negated, and bad-regex filters are not coloured.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Sun, 14 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The --web browser UI reaches feature parity with the terminal viewer: log-level
    filter chips, a drag-to-filter time histogram, per-line JSON pretty-print and
    wrap (variable-height rows), per-term hit counts, a "copy as shell command"
    (grep/awk) export, a keyboard-shortcuts help overlay, a recent-search dropdown,
    a four-lane minimap (bookmarks/matches/ranges/selected), double-click to anchor
    a line, and Zebra/Minimap/Histogram display toggles. All view state (now
    including level and time-range filters) stays in the URL as the --view token, so
    every view remains a shareable link. Still loopback-only, still no new runtime
    dependencies.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Sat, 13 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New --web mode: open a log in a local browser tab instead of the TUI
    (loopback-only HTTP, --web-port to pin the port). It reuses zerch's engine
    and view model and offers clickable filters, highlights, bookmarks, live
    search with n/N navigation, a minimap, hide/reveal, and horizontal scrolling
    for long lines. The whole view lives in the URL as the same --view token, so
    every view is a shareable link and each tab is independent; the view is saved
    per file between runs, as in the TUI. Vanilla JS/CSS baked into the binary,
    no new runtime dependencies (tiny_http, no TLS backend).

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Sat, 13 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Hide Columns and Bookmarks menu fields now accept inclusive ranges:
    "1,3-5,8" is the same as "1,3,4,5,8". Reversed ranges are ignored and each
    range is capped so a typo can't balloon memory.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Per-file sessions: each file's view (filters, highlights, bookmarks, hidden
    lines, search, and the cursor line) is saved on exit and restored on the
    next run (--fresh opens clean, ZERCH_NO_SESSION=1 disables). A numeric prefix
    before the arrows pans by that many columns. Field hiding: inline-editable
    Separator and Hide Columns menu fields blank chosen columns with an ellipsis.
    The Bookmarks menu entry is now inline-editable, and the syntax-colour toggle
    is saved in the --view string.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.4.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hide specific lines: press "x" on a line to hide it (it collapses into a
    gap). Reveal the gap or press "X" in the menu to bring hidden lines back.
    Hidden lines are saved in the --view string.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.4.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Vim-style navigation: H/M/L move the cursor to the top/middle/bottom of the
    visible screen, ":N" jumps to line N (":$" to the last line), and n/N now
    step to the next/previous match relative to the cursor.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remember the last 100 search / filter / highlight terms across sessions
    (recall with the up/down arrows), like less. Stored owner-readable only at
    $XDG_STATE_HOME/zerch/history (override with $ZERCH_HISTFILE; "-" disables).

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Sun, 03 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed the project from "zercher" to "zerch" — shorter to type and a
    clearer nod to "search". The binary, crate, man page, and package are all
    now "zerch"; no functional changes.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read logs from stdin ('zerch -' or a pipe, less-style), spooled to a
    temp file and indexed as usual. The menu now shows a hit-count per filter
    and highlight, computed lazily in the background so the first page still
    appears instantly. Duplicate filter/highlight terms are rejected. Various
    fixes: syntax coloring of unquoted values like a=1,b=2, 'q' now exits the
    histogram brush, the cursor stays centered when toggling wrap, and piped
    input works on macOS.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000

zerch (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Faster indexing (parallel newline scan, ~15x on large files), ~50% less
    per-line metadata memory, editable input line with shared history and
    inline regex/case toggles for search/filter/highlight, syntax coloring
    for logfmt and JSON, Ctrl-Z suspend, height-aware wrap scrolling, and
    various bug fixes. Native Debian source package now included.

 -- Adi Zaimi <adizaimi@yahoo.com>  Mon, 07 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000

